{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966811,"nonce":"Gw70MXbXHQdfYWIIlL4vv1E1W9k=","title":"Zyntax's Cranelift backend only widened int-vs-int binary operands, so an int literal in a","message":"`computed { pct.get() + radius.get() + 2 } : f64` in a `.blinc` file\nproduced a Cranelift verifier error and then\n`CreateClosure: Lambda function HirId(...) not found`. Nothing failed at\nthe call site: the computed just never produced a value.\n\nCause: the live binary-op lowering in\n`zyntax/crates/compiler/src/cranelift_backend.rs` picked the instruction\nfrom the HIR result type but only reconciled operands when BOTH were\nintegers. An untyped literal in a float expression is an `iconst.i32`,\nso `fadd.f64 v5, v2` reached the verifier.\n\nFixed with `reconcile_binary_operands` + `convert_numeric`. Note\n`convert_numeric` is deliberately separate from the existing\n`coerce_value`, which bitcasts when the widths match — right for an ABI\nslot, wrong for arithmetic, since `2i64` reinterpreted as `f64` is not\n`2.0`.\n\nThe other three `HirInstruction::Binary` lowering sites in that file are\n`#[allow(dead_code)]`; only the one inside the block-walking loop is\nlive.","files":null}]}